WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.429
Welcome to the Grounded
Synthetic Respondent Lab.

2
00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:06.066
It's a place to practice market research

3
00:00:06.066 --> 00:00:09.624
with AI respondents before
you talk to real customers.

4
00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:14.040
We built it at Cal Poly Pomona with
Dr. Fan Wang and Dr. Yufan Lin.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.335
First, turn on the Demo
(no AI) switch at the top.

6
00:00:17.335 --> 00:00:20.499
It replays saved answers,
so nothing is charged.

7
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.453
Under Set Up, choose the Neo
Smart Living guided demo.

8
00:00:24.453 --> 00:00:27.496
One click fills in every
step for a real product,

9
00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:30.352
a small backyard studio
called the Tahoe Mini.

10
00:00:30.352 --> 00:00:33.457
A custom study starts blank,
for your own product.

11
00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:37.414
Audience says who you want
to hear from: location,

12
00:00:37.414 --> 00:00:40.233
age, income, home ownership and lifestyle.

13
00:00:40.233 --> 00:00:43.588
Respondent traits are drawn
from US Census tables,

14
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:47.011
so the mix of ages, incomes
and homes is realistic.

15
00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:52.309
Product describes what people are
reacting to: the business, the product,

16
00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:56.235
its price range, key features,
use cases and likely concerns.

17
00:00:56.235 --> 00:00:59.646
Every respondent reads this
context before answering.

18
00:01:00.247 --> 00:01:03.452
Market adds the alternatives
people compare against,

19
00:01:03.452 --> 00:01:06.040
like a shed conversion or a home addition,

20
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.231
plus the features they expect and
the objections they usually raise.

21
00:01:10.832 --> 00:01:12.814
Survey holds the questionnaire.

22
00:01:12.814 --> 00:01:15.628
The guided demo loads
the Tahoe Mini survey,

23
00:01:15.628 --> 00:01:18.953
or you can upload your own
as Markdown, Word or PDF.

24
00:01:18.953 --> 00:01:21.191
You can also add your own question.

25
00:01:21.191 --> 00:01:25.540
I'll ask how interested people would
be in solar panels on the roof,

26
00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.011
on a one to five scale.

27
00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.484
Experiment sets the sample
size and the models.

28
00:01:30.484 --> 00:01:35.131
You can mix models and pick Split Sample
to divide respondents between them,

29
00:01:35.131 --> 00:01:38.311
or Mirror to have each model
answer the same people.

30
00:01:38.311 --> 00:01:41.674
I'll ask for one hundred
respondents and save the plan.

31
00:01:42.323 --> 00:01:46.570
With Demo on, Run live is locked,
so I'll show the preloaded demo.

32
00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.401
These are one hundred
synthetic respondents,

33
00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:54.549
answered earlier by four models that drew
each answer from the odds they stated.

34
00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:55.578
No AI is called.

35
00:01:55.578 --> 00:01:59.632
My solar question isn't in that
saved run; it needs a live run.

36
00:02:00.233 --> 00:02:03.385
Result turns every question
into a small dashboard.

37
00:02:03.385 --> 00:02:05.424
You can read the overall answers,

38
00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:09.132
or filter by model to see how
one model answered on its own.

39
00:02:09.732 --> 00:02:13.121
Insights pulls the signals
together: the leading use case,

40
00:02:13.121 --> 00:02:16.919
the heaviest barriers, and which
concepts lift purchase interest.

41
00:02:16.919 --> 00:02:19.198
Read it as directional, not a forecast.

42
00:02:19.198 --> 00:02:21.769
It tells you what to
check with real people.

43
00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:24.826
Now I turn Demo off and press Run live.

44
00:02:24.826 --> 00:02:27.911
With the class key set,
the guided demo uses Jev,

45
00:02:27.911 --> 00:02:29.485
which answers every scale

46
00:02:29.485 --> 00:02:32.948
and choice question by drawing
from the odds it states.

47
00:02:32.948 --> 00:02:35.656
One hundred respondents
take a few seconds,

48
00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:38.363
and every answer comes
live from the model.

49
00:02:38.363 --> 00:02:41.952
In Result, my solar panel
question now has its own chart.

50
00:02:41.952 --> 00:02:45.101
Then I turn Demo back on
for the rest of the tour.

51
00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.129
Interview runs synthetic depth interviews
with the same kind of personas.

52
00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:53.041
In the guided demo these
are seeded transcripts,

53
00:02:53.041 --> 00:02:55.711
so no model is called,
and the page says so.

54
00:02:55.711 --> 00:02:58.441
You can open each
transcript pair to read it.

55
00:02:59.042 --> 00:03:03.045
The Research Brief frames what you
want to learn: your main question,

56
00:03:03.045 --> 00:03:06.758
your hypotheses, and the decisions
the interviews should inform.

57
00:03:06.758 --> 00:03:09.775
It tells the insights step
which themes matter most.

58
00:03:10.376 --> 00:03:14.031
Interview Insights groups the
transcripts into recurring themes,

59
00:03:14.031 --> 00:03:15.916
each with a representative quote.

60
00:03:15.916 --> 00:03:20.085
With a live key, you can also keep
interviewing any persona in character.

61
00:03:20.686 --> 00:03:23.696
Student Interview is a
separate page for class.

62
00:03:23.696 --> 00:03:27.089
Each persona is one household
drawn from Census data.

63
00:03:27.089 --> 00:03:31.572
Students pick one, ask their own
questions, and export the transcript.

64
00:03:31.572 --> 00:03:35.542
In demo mode it plays back
pre-recorded interviews at no cost.

65
00:03:36.142 --> 00:03:38.949
Focus Group puts you in
the moderator's seat.

66
00:03:38.949 --> 00:03:42.629
The personas hear each other
and react, across five stages,

67
00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:45.998
from an icebreaker through
price reactions to a close.

68
00:03:45.998 --> 00:03:49.179
You tag quotes into themes
and write your own memo.

69
00:03:49.179 --> 00:03:51.425
The demo replays a recorded session.

70
00:03:52.024 --> 00:03:56.728
That's the whole loop: set up, survey,
run, read the results, and interview.

71
00:03:56.728 --> 00:03:59.204
These answers are a rehearsal, not data.

72
00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:01.370
Use them to sharpen your questions,

73
00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:06.507
and always compare what the AI says with
real customers before you decide anything.

74
00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:10.592
The student team behind the lab is
Anderson Edmond, Minh and Yaza.
